          "note_id": "ihKwhpYZkca",
          "fields": {
            "display_title": "The paper is about open domain QA. It describes an interesting approach to train the retriever using attention of the reader as weak supervision signal. This helps solve the problem of lack of QA-oriented text retrieval relevance judgments. The general assumption is that the reader can provide useful signals back to the reader. The experiments on 2 datasets confirm that such a process can indeed help increase the performance.",
            "replying_to": "Replying to Distilling Knowledge from Reader to Retriever for Question Answering"
